  "kind": "capacity",
  "date": "2026-09-17",
  "title": "The gemm task had no applicable dot contract on gfx938; declaring one changed nothing, and the campaign still lowers a contraction with no matrix instruction",
  "backend": "triton-dcu",
  "target": "gfx938",
  "compiler_revision_id": "open-cake-ir@4278caf2",
  "executor_revision": "gfx938@b85c696a",
  "evidence": {
    "retained": "bw1100 /home/testuser01/oci-dcu-runs/gemm-20260917-225918, protocol_adherence adhered, endpoint qualified_by_budget true, best_confirmed_latency_ms 0.409279; gemm-20260918-042832, run at the commit that declares the fp32 contracts, adhered and qualified",
    "sites": [
      "the run's candidate artifacts -- lowered_source, ttir, ttgir and amdgcn all contain zero tl.dot, zero mma operations and no v_mmac mnemonic",
      "src/open_cake_ir/tasks/contraction/authoring.py:65 -- the gemm starter, identical in shape on every target: fp32 tensors and a reduce over an elementwise product, with no tl.dot and no instruction contract on any backend, B300 included",
      "compiler/targets/gfx938.json -- dot contracts triton.dot.fp16_fp32 and triton.dot.fp8e4m3_fp32, and no fp32 form",
      "compiler/targets/sm_103a.json -- declares triton.dot.fp32_ieee and triton.dot.fp32_tf32 alongside its reduced-precision forms",
      "measured through Compiler.assess: the gfx938 mma corpus case with its operands moved to fp32 is refused, accepted=False",
      "gemm-20260918-042832 candidate artifacts -- still zero tl.dot, zero mma operations and no v_mmac, and best_confirmed_latency_ms 0.409279, the same value as the run before the contracts existed"
    ]
  },
  "observation": [
    "An earlier version of this record said the author had the declaration and did not reach for it. That was wrong, and the correction is the finding.\n\nThe gemm task is fp32 -- the starter declares fp32 tensors on every target and contracts a reduce over an elementwise product. gfx938 declares dot contracts for fp16 and fp8e4m3 and for nothing else. So no admitted contract covers this workload's dtype, and a contraction written with one would have been refused: the gfx938 mma corpus case with its operands moved to fp32 assesses accepted=False. The author did not decline an available instruction; there was none available for what it was asked to compute.\n\nThat the reference bundle names both contracts is what made this look like a choice. It names what the Target declares, not what applies to the case in hand, and the two differ here by dtype alone.\n\nThe neighbouring fact is that the starter carries no tl.dot on any target, B300 included, so nothing here shows the DCU behaving differently from the incumbent -- only that the DCU cannot yet be asked to. sm_103a declares triton.dot.fp32_ieee and triton.dot.fp32_tf32; gfx938 declares no fp32 form because none has been measured on it, which is the correct state for an undeclared fact and not a defect.",
    "\n",
    "\n",
