  "proposed_change": "Do not widen anything to force it; the candidate is correct and the run adherent. The open question is narrower than it was: with the contract available and unused, the remaining candidate explanation is that nothing in the authoring environment shows a contraction on this target using one.\n\nTesting that means changing the starter or adding a worked Corpus example, which changes the treatment: campaigns before and after are not matched, and that boundary has to be recorded rather than absorbed. It is worth doing deliberately, because the alternative is a target that declares a matrix unit no campaign ever reaches.\n\nWhat this record should not be read as: evidence that the model cannot use mma. One task, one shape, two runs. The contracts are declared and gate-covered now, so the next campaign that wants one is not blocked by the Compiler.",
  "decision": "open",
  "implemented_in": "open-cake-ir@c70dcfcf",
  "verified_by": "the fp32 probe on a BW1101 -- v_mmac_16x16x8_f32 for ieee with max_abs_error 0, v_mmac_f32_16x16x8_tf32 for tf32 at 7.177e-04 relative, no v_fma in either -- and Corpus case gfx938-gemm-bias-mma-fp32-accepted, which lowers to tl.dot(..., input_precision=\"ieee\")"
}
